          5.SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE

EduGenie follows a simple application architecture where the user interacts with the frontend and requests are processed by the Python application and AI components.


1.User Layer

The user layer represents students who interact with the EduGenie application. Students can:
     * Enter questions
     * Request learning assistance
     * Interact with AI
     * Access generated educational content


2.Frontend / Interface Layer

The frontend provides the interface through which students interact with EduGenie. This layer is responsible for:

     * User interaction
     * Input collection
     * Displaying AI responses
     * Presenting learning content


3.Backend Layer

The backend processes user requests and manages the application logic. Python is used for implementing the backend functionality. It is responsible for:

     * Processing user requests
     * Managing application logic
     * Communicating with AI services
     * Returning responses to the user


4.AI Layer

The AI layer provides intelligent processing and response generation. It can be used to:

     * Understand student questions
     * Generate responses
     * Explain concepts
     * Assist with learning content
     * Data Layer

The data layer can be used to store application-related information. Future implementation can include:

      * Student information
      * Learning history
      * Questions
      * Generated content
      * Student progress


         6.BACKEND ARCHITECTURE

The backend is responsible for processing user requests and connecting the application with AI functionality. The major backend responsibilities include:

     * Request processing
     * Input handling
     * AI communication
     * Response generation
     * Error handling
     * Application logic

Python provides the main programming environment for the backend implementation. The backend flow can be represented as:

           User Interface
                ↓
             Backend
                ↓
           AI Processing
                ↓
             Response
                ↓
               User


This modular approach makes the project easier to maintain and extend.


